  "rules": [
    "GPIO34, GPIO35, GPIO36 and GPIO39 are input-only and have no internal pull-up or pull-down.",
    "GPIO6 to GPIO11 are connected to the internal SPI flash and must not be used.",
    "GPIO0 is the BOOT pin: it must be high at power-on; holding it low enters the bootloader.",
    "GPIO0, GPIO2, GPIO5, GPIO12 and GPIO15 are strapping pins: an attached circuit must not force the wrong level at power-on.",
    "GPIO12 must be low at power-on; pulling it high selects 1.8 V flash and can prevent booting.",
    "GPIO1 and GPIO3 are UART0 and are shared with USB serial; using them conflicts with the Serial Monitor.",
    "ADC2 channels cannot be read while Wi-Fi is active; prefer ADC1 channels (GPIO32 to GPIO39) for analog input.",
    "ESP32 GPIO is 3.3 V logic and is not 5 V tolerant; a 5 V signal needs level shifting before a GPIO input.",
    "EN is the reset/enable line and is not a GPIO.",
    "Power and ground pins are not GPIO."
  ],
